      "content": "A business expense, like the high-quality ergonomic chair, is generally appropriate if you can demonstrate it's used for business purposes, even if it's in your home studio. You need to keep good records, like a detailed receipt, to prove it's for your work, not just for general comfort. If you use it primarily for business tasks, it's a deductible expense. If you can't clearly separate its use, you might need to prorate the deduction based on business use percentage.",
